Referenced community projects
-----------------------------

1. Mr-Pian/Deepcool-Bingyu-serise-software-for-linux
   https://github.com/Mr-Pian/Deepcool-Bingyu-serise-software-for-linux
   License: MIT
   Role: prior art of the same protocol family. It documents the
   DeepCool Bingyu LT/LS variant (USB 3633:0026, 320x240 RGB565 raw
   frames). SPARTACUS-linux implements a different, independently
   developed variant (USB 3633:0027, 480x480, JPEG push).
   No source code was copied from this project; it was studied for
   handshake/reset patterns and general device behaviour.

2. liquidctl (Jon Sparkes / Callum Stewart et al.)
   https://github.com/liquidctl/liquidctl
   License: GPLv3
   Role: general insight into DeepCool USB peripheral protocols and
   the Linux userspace approach. No code was copied or linked.

